<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<div xmlns:ead="https://archivists.org/ns/ead/v4" xmlns:eac="http://archivists.org/ns/eac/v2" xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3c.org/1999/xlink" type="elementDocumentation" xml:id="elem-dimensions">
	<head>
		<gi>dimensions</gi>
	</head>
	<div type="fullName">
		<p>Dimensions</p>
	</div>
	<div type="summary">
		<p>A child element of <gi>formAvailable</gi> that provides information about the size of the material being described.</p>
	</div>
	<div type="mayContain">
		<p>
			<list type="gloss">
				<label>quantity</label>
				<item>0..1</item>
				<label>unitOfMeasurement</label>
				<item>0..1</item>
			</list>
		</p>
	</div>
	<div type="mayOccurWithin">
		<p>formAvailable</p>
	</div>
	<div type="attributes">
    		<p>
			<list type="gloss">
            			<label>audience</label>
            			<item>Optional</item>
           			<label>conventionDeclarationReference</label>
            			<item>Optional</item>
            			<label>id</label>
            			<item>Optional</item>
            			<label>languageOfElement</label>
            			<item>Optional</item>
				<label>localType</label>
            			<item>Optional</item>
            			<label>localTypeDeclarationReference</label>
            			<item>Optional</item>
				<label>maintenanceEventReference</label>
            			<item>Optional</item>
            			<label>scriptOfElement</label>
            			<item>Optional</item>
            			<label>sourceReference</label>
            			<item>Optional</item>
            			<label>target</label>
            			<item>Optional</item>
			</list>
    		</p>
	</div>
	<div type="description">
		<p><gi>dimensions</gi> may be used to specify the size, in two or three dimensions, of the units identified within <gi>extent</gi>. It usually includes numerical data. Express measurements in any convenient unit as indicated in the <gi>unitOfMeasurement</gi> sub-element of <gi>dimensions</gi>, for example, "inches" or "centimeters.". Multiple dimensions, for example, height-by-width, can be encoded in a single <gi>dimensions</gi> or in separate <gi>dimensions</gi> with distinctive <att>localType</att> values.</p>
		<p>Either the sub-element <gi>quantity</gi> or the sub-element <gi>unitOfMeasurement</gi> must be present within <gi>dimensions</gi>, but it is recommended to use both child elements whenever possible.</p>
	</div>
	<div type="availability">
		<p>Optional, repeatable</p>
	</div>
	<div type="examples">
		<egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples">
			<!-- Contains examples of XML from the schema.  Tags in egXML must be prefixed with the proper namespace (e.g. <ead:unittitle> -->
		</egXML>
	</div>
</div>
